<section id="methodology">
  <h2>Methodology &amp; Data Quality Notes</h2>
  <p><strong>Dataset:</strong> 4,886 biomedical research abstracts sourced from PubMed (Kaggle: kanchana1990/biomedical-research-abstracts-20242026), covering January 2024 to March 2026. Columns include PMID, title, abstract, journal, publication date, author count, country, research type, MeSH keywords, major topic, and open-access flag.</p>
  <p><strong>Temporal skew:</strong> Approximately 80% of records are from 2024. This is a known PubMed indexing artifact, not a data error. Year-over-year comparisons use both raw counts and normalized shares where appropriate.</p>
  <p><strong>Missing data:</strong> 2,303 records (47.1%) lack MeSH keywords or major topics, and 754 (15.4%) lack month-level metadata. These gaps are concentrated in 2025–2026 and reflect incomplete indexing for recent publications.</p>
  <p><strong>Country cleaning:</strong> Obvious duplicates (e.g., "PR China" → "China", "United States" → "USA") were merged. Long or institution-like strings were retained as originally labeled; only exact duplicates were standardized.</p>
  <p><strong>Research type classification:</strong> Multi-value PubMed publication types were simplified to a single primary category using hierarchical rules: Case Report > Systematic Review > Review > Journal Article > Other.</p>
  <p><strong>Open access definition:</strong> Based on the boolean <code>open_access</code> field, which indicates PMC availability. This may undercount gold OA in journals not deposited to PMC.</p>
